# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 508 Filmzz — build-time configuration
#
# The site is a STATIC EXPORT on GitHub Pages. There is no server at runtime, so
# nothing here is a secret — every NEXT_PUBLIC_ value is compiled into the
# browser bundle and is visible to anyone.
#
# Your actual credentials (Twilio, Gmail, the Sheet) live in Google Apps Script
# under Project Settings → Script Properties. They are never in this repo, which
# is what makes a public repository safe. See docs/GITHUB-PAGES.md.
#
# In production these are set as GitHub repository *variables*:
#   Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables
# Locally, copy this file to .env.local.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. Booking form endpoint ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Apps Script Web app URL — Deploy → New deployment → Web app, with
# "Who has access" set to Anyone. Looks like:
#   https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfy.../exec
#
# Leave blank and the form stays visible but tells visitors to call or email
# instead of silently failing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT=


# ── 2. Base path ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave blank for the custom domain (www.508filmzz.com), which serves at the
# root. Only set this to preview at <user>.github.io/<repo>, where the site
# lives under a subpath — and remove public/CNAME if you do.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Search visibility  ← THE SOFT-LAUNCH SWITCH
#
# Unset or anything except "true"  → site is LIVE but NOINDEX. Anyone with the
#                                     link sees it; Google never lists it.
# "true"                           → site is fully indexable.
#
# Fail-closed on purpose: a typo keeps you private rather than accidentally
# public. Read at BUILD time, so you must re-run the deploy workflow after
# changing it — editing the variable alone does nothing.
#
# Verify after deploy:  curl -s https://www.508filmzz.com/robots.txt
#   private → "Disallow: /"      public → "Allow: /"
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_INDEXABLE=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Analytics & verification
#
# All optional. Each tag renders only when its variable is set, so leaving these
# blank ships zero third-party JavaScript. NEXT_PUBLIC_ vars are exposed to the
# browser by design — never put a secret in one.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 4. Google Search Console ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# search.google.com/search-console → Add property (URL prefix) → HTML tag.
# Paste ONLY the content="..." value, not the whole meta tag.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# ── 5. Google Analytics 4 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# analytics.google.com → Admin → Data Streams → your stream → Measurement ID.
# Leave blank if you run GA4 through GTM instead — setting both double-counts
# every pageview.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=

# ── 6. Google Tag Manager ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tagmanager.google.com → container ID, format GTM-XXXXXXX.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# ── 7. Microsoft Clarity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# clarity.microsoft.com → Settings → Overview → Project ID.
# Free heatmaps and session recordings — genuinely useful on a portfolio site
# for seeing how far people scroll before they bounce.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=

# ── 8. Meta Pixel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# business.facebook.com → Events Manager → Data Sources → your pixel → ID.
# Only needed if you run Facebook/Instagram ads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
